[Music]  the eu  has helped make european shipping  cleaners safer and fairer  [Music]  in 1986 a level playing field for  shipping companies was created thanks to  european legislation  it removed barriers for operators  counted protectionism from countries  outside the block  and made pricing fairer  further liberalization of the transport  and passenger markets came in 1992  relaxing rules in the short haul market  this allowed companies from one country  in the block  to sail between the ports of another  member state  at the turn of the millennium not one  but two disasters struck which would  shape eu maritime legislation  in 1999 the oil tanker erica sank near  france  prestige another tanker full of heavy  oil sank near spain  three years later the environmental  catastrophes led to the creation of the  eu maritime agency  and better compensation for the victims  of oil spills  that legislation included the  introduction of stronger hulls for  tankers  stricter mandatory inspections  blacklisting dangerous ships from eu  ports  and black box data recorders  [Music]  parliament backed rules making shipping  even safer in 2003  increasing standards in both passenger  and cargo transport  better protecting people and the  environment against accidents and  negligence  [Music]  preventives  in 2005 as europe's roads became  increasingly congested with lorry  traffic  parliament called for short-haul  shipping as an alternative to road  transport  then it backed gradually reducing toxic  sulfur in marine fuel in 2012  as part of the drive to save lives and  make the shipping industry cleaner  data nuclear library and i had to be an  ill mass australian  today shipping still accounts for about  2.5 percent of global greenhouse gas  emissions  parliament is calling for climate  neutral eu maritime transport by 2050  with clean ports the phasing out of  heavy oil and more research  into green technologies and fuels

